00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:23.520
Good morning everyone. I'm Jayon from

00:18:21.039 --> 00:18:25.760
the University of Cambridge. Today I

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:28.559
will introduce a new single stage

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:33.720
vertical 48 volt to core power delivery

00:18:28.559 --> 00:18:33.720
architecture for future AI processors.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:39.039
So first why do we need a single stage

00:18:36.559 --> 00:18:42.080
conversion? The first reason is

00:18:39.039 --> 00:18:44.799
efficiency. Compared with a traditional

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:47.760
two-stage architecture, the single stage

00:18:44.799 --> 00:18:49.840
conversion removes the intermediate bus

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:53.600
and can improve the end to end

00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:56.080
efficiency by about 2 percentage point.

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:59.320
At data center scale, this can make a

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:59.320
big difference.

00:18:59.919 --> 00:19:05.440
But efficiency is not the only issue. As

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:07.440
processor power increase, the low

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:10.880
voltage bus also becomes more

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:15.200
challenging to scale. Take the WSC3 as

00:19:10.880 --> 00:19:19.760
an example. Its power is about 23 kilow.

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:23.600
So a 6 W bus carries about 3.8 kilo

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:25.919
amps. For such a large processor power,

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:29.360
it's quite difficult to keep the

00:19:25.919 --> 00:19:32.559
distribution resistance very low. Even

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:35.039
with zero even with only 0.1 milliohm

00:19:32.559 --> 00:19:38.720
resistance, the conduction loss is

00:19:35.039 --> 00:19:41.280
already about 1.47 kilowatt.

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:43.200
This is unacceptable for practical power

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:46.160
delivery.

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:48.559
Besides, a low voltage bus also stores

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:51.360
less energy. So more decoupling

00:19:48.559 --> 00:19:54.080
capacitance are required which takes up

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:57.280
valuable B area.

00:19:54.080 --> 00:20:02.039
That's why we prefer to keep 48 volts as

00:19:57.280 --> 00:20:02.039
the border level distribution wattage.

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:08.080
From 48 volts, there are two passes to

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:10.799
the core. One is direct to core

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:12.960
conversion and the other is the AVR

00:20:10.799 --> 00:20:16.960
based architecture

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:20.240
where a front end VRM generates a 1.8

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:24.320
regulated voltage and the AVR performs

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:28.000
the final regulation close die. So in

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:32.360
this case our single CVM can also serves

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:32.360
as the AVR front end.

00:20:33.039 --> 00:20:38.640
Based on this system architecture, we

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:41.039
propose a single stage vertical VM.

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:43.440
Actually, it has four main features.

00:20:41.039 --> 00:20:46.320
Single stage conversion, vertical power

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:50.120
delivery, direct topside cooling, and

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:50.120
the modular scalability.

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:55.840
To achieve this, the converter must have

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:58.559
high conversion ratio and high output

00:20:55.840 --> 00:21:00.720
current capability. We therefore choose

00:20:58.559 --> 00:21:02.880
the Hbridgeidge current douler topology

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:04.720
with fractional turns.

00:21:02.880 --> 00:21:06.799
The operation modes are showing on the

00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:09.440
right but I will not go into the details

00:21:06.799 --> 00:21:12.159
here.

00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:15.200
From the operation mode we can find the

00:21:12.159 --> 00:21:18.320
two different current loops. First as

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:20.720
shown on the left top the high frequency

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:23.600
AC current remains within the

00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:26.240
transformer and rectifier stage and this

00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:30.159
current does not flow directly to the

00:21:26.240 --> 00:21:33.440
load. So for this loop the main design

00:21:30.159 --> 00:21:37.679
goal is to keep the high car is to keep

00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:42.000
the primary and secondary high coupling.

00:21:37.679 --> 00:21:44.320
So we use a closely interlar windings to

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:48.320
reduce liquid inductance and the winding

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:51.760
loss. In contrast as shown on the bottom

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:55.360
the inductor DC current is flow directly

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:58.240
to the load. So for this loop the main

00:21:55.360 --> 00:22:01.760
design goal is to keep the high current

00:21:58.240 --> 00:22:04.240
conduction path as short as possible. We

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:07.600
therefore route the DC current

00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:10.159
vertically to the load. So this leads to

00:22:07.600 --> 00:22:12.720
the model structure showing on the right

00:22:10.159 --> 00:22:16.000
a planer transformer in the center with

00:22:12.720 --> 00:22:18.000
vertical inductors on both sides.

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:21.120
We also selected different material

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:24.000
magnetic materials to to satisfy

00:22:21.120 --> 00:22:27.760
different requirements. For AC flux we

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:30.320
choose ferite for low loss and for DC

00:22:27.760 --> 00:22:33.120
flux you mean for the inductor we choose

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:37.320
powder core for higher saturation and

00:22:33.120 --> 00:22:37.320
high output current capability.

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:43.760
We can further integrate the transformer

00:22:41.039 --> 00:22:46.880
and the inductors by sharing part of the

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:49.840
magnetic core. This works because the

00:22:46.880 --> 00:22:52.400
two flux passes are nearly orthogonal.

00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:55.600
So the interaction between them is quite

00:22:52.400 --> 00:22:58.480
small. Here we look at their two flux

00:22:55.600 --> 00:23:02.159
passes after integration. From the side

00:22:58.480 --> 00:23:05.120
view we can find the transformer AC flux

00:23:02.159 --> 00:23:08.159
closed through the ferite core and part

00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:11.679
of the powder core. And from the top

00:23:08.159 --> 00:23:15.200
view we can find the inductor flux

00:23:11.679 --> 00:23:17.919
remains within the powder core. So even

00:23:15.200 --> 00:23:21.039
after integration the two magnetic

00:23:17.919 --> 00:23:22.960
functions are still valented. The model

00:23:21.039 --> 00:23:24.960
structure is showing on the is showing

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:27.440
on the right is similar with the

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:30.440
previous one but with more integrated

00:23:27.440 --> 00:23:30.440
magnetics.

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:37.200
Besides this architecture also provides

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:40.159
us more flexibility in the inductor

00:23:37.200 --> 00:23:43.360
design. We can either use the direct

00:23:40.159 --> 00:23:46.320
negative coupling or TR based indirect

00:23:43.360 --> 00:23:49.960
coupling and both case can improve the

00:23:46.320 --> 00:23:49.960
transient response.

00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:55.679
Based on this concept, we built a

00:23:52.880 --> 00:23:59.520
prototype to validate the single stage

00:23:55.679 --> 00:24:02.080
conversion. It converts 54 volts to 0.8

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:04.880
volts directly and achieves a current

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:07.679
density about 1.5 amps per square

00:24:04.880 --> 00:24:09.600
millmter. And overall it's more

00:24:07.679 --> 00:24:12.600
efficient than a traditional two-c

00:24:09.600 --> 00:24:12.600
architecture.

00:24:13.440 --> 00:24:18.559
Finally, let's look at how this

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:20.960
architecture can scale to multi kilo amp

00:24:18.559 --> 00:24:24.400
processor power delivery.

00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:28.320
From the system level, 800 W is firstly

00:24:24.400 --> 00:24:32.000
converted to a 48 volt and then 48 volt

00:24:28.320 --> 00:24:34.640
is distributed across the IT board

00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:37.840
around each processor. Multiple single

00:24:34.640 --> 00:24:40.320
CD RMS can work in parallel under

00:24:37.840 --> 00:24:42.799
standard digital mass phase control like

00:24:40.320 --> 00:24:45.360
the PWM control

00:24:42.799 --> 00:24:48.000
and they can also be placed directly

00:24:45.360 --> 00:24:51.440
underneath the processor also multiple

00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:53.279
uh where in parallel and in this case

00:24:51.440 --> 00:24:56.000
the high current conduction path can be

00:24:53.279 --> 00:24:58.159
very short

00:24:56.000 --> 00:25:02.120
that's the idea of single stage VM.

